{
  "entry": {
    "title": "Battle of Greenhill",
    "description": "The Battle of Greenhill was one of the first major confrontations of the Hundred-Year War. It took place in a fertile valley known for its lush green fields, which became the battlefield for a clash between a coalition of human and dwarven forces against the High Elves. The humans and dwarves, led by General Markus and Thrain Ironfist, hoped to secure Greenhill as a strategic foothold. The High Elves, under General Elenion, approached with a smaller, highly trained force. Using their superior magical abilities, the High Elves decimated the coalition forces, establishing their dominance early in the conflict. Despite valiant efforts, the humans and dwarves were unable to withstand the magical onslaught, leading to a decisive elven victory."
  }
}

{
  "entry": {
    "title": "Battle of Whispering Woods",
    "description": "The Battle of Whispering Woods was a pivotal encounter showcasing the Wood Elves' expertise in guerrilla warfare. The dense, ancient forest served as the perfect battleground for the Wood Elves, led by the legendary archer Trelisia. The human army, commanded by General Alistair, entered the forest cautiously but underestimated the Wood Elves' capabilities. The Wood Elves launched a series of hit-and-run attacks, using the terrain to their advantage. After days of relentless assaults, the human army was forced to retreat in disarray. The Wood Elves' victory defended their homeland and inflicted heavy casualties on the human forces."
  }
}

{
